IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fta-types`
IMPORT `fta-transactions`

-- Fair Trading Act 1986 — GOAL 4: ENFORCEMENT.
--
--   "Is a contravention an offence; what is the maximum fine; is it an
--    infringement offence; by when must a s 43 order be sought; may the
--    District Court or Disputes Tribunal make it; and the banning orders."
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_121.txt — Part 5,
-- ss 37-46M, and ss 47F, 47J.

§ `Goal 4 — enforcement`

§§ `Offences and fines (ss 4, 40)`

DECLARE `Part of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `Part 1`
    `Part 2`
    `Part 3`
    `Part 4`
    `Part 4A`

@ref ss 7-36ZF
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition
GIVETH A `Part of the Act`
`the Part containing` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `s 28 a consumer information standard`          THEN `Part 2`
    WHEN `s 28B disclosing trader status online`         THEN `Part 2`
    WHEN `s 30 a product safety standard`                THEN `Part 3`
    WHEN `s 31 supplying goods under an unsafe goods notice` THEN `Part 3`
    WHEN `s 31A not notifying a voluntary recall`        THEN `Part 3`
    WHEN `s 32 a compulsory recall notice`               THEN `Part 3`
    WHEN `s 33D a suspension of supply notice`           THEN `Part 3`
    WHEN `s 36 a services safety standard`               THEN `Part 4`
    WHEN `s 36C or 36D layby disclosure`                 THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36F a layby cancellation charge`             THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36L uninvited direct sale disclosure`        THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36RA entering or not leaving residential premises` THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36U extended warranty disclosure`            THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36WB a gift card expiring in less than 3 years` THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36WC a gift card without a prominent expiry` THEN `Part 4A`
    WHEN `s 36ZB, 36ZD or 36ZF auction duties`           THEN `Part 4A`
    OTHERWISE `Part 1`

-- s 40 "(1) Every person who contravenes a provision of Part 1 (except
-- sections 9, 14(2), 23, or 24), Part 3, or Part 4 commits an offence and is
-- liable on conviction,— (a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not
-- exceeding $200,000; and (b) in the case of a body corporate, to a fine not
-- exceeding $600,000. (1A) Every person who contravenes section 24 commits
-- an offence and is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $600,000.
-- (1B) Every person who contravenes a provision of Part 2 or Part 4A commits
-- an offence and is liable on conviction,— (a) in the case of an
-- individual, to a fine not exceeding $10,000; and (b) in the case of a body
-- corporate, to a fine not exceeding $30,000." s 4(2) "The Crown shall not be
-- liable to be prosecuted for an offence against this Act".
@ref ss 4(2), 40
@export The maximum fine for a contravention of the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ) under s 40: Part 1 (except ss 9, 14(2), 23 and 24), Part 3 and Part 4, $200,000 for an individual and $600,000 for a body corporate; s 24 (pyramid selling), $600,000; Part 2 and Part 4A, $10,000 and $30,000; ss 9, 14(2) and 23 are not offences (0); the Crown is not prosecuted (0). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition  @desc The provision contravened
      kind IS A `Kind of person`  @desc An individual or a body corporate
      crown IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person is the Crown
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for contravening` p `, by` kind `, the Crown:` crown MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF crown THEN 0
        IF    p EQUALS `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade`
           OR p EQUALS `s 14(2) force, harassment or coercion about land`
           OR p EQUALS `s 23 harassment or coercion`
            THEN 0
        IF p EQUALS `s 24 promoting or operating a pyramid selling scheme` THEN 600000
        IF `the Part containing` p EQUALS `Part 2` OR `the Part containing` p EQUALS `Part 4A`
            THEN IF kind EQUALS `an individual` THEN 10000 ELSE 30000
        OTHERWISE IF kind EQUALS `an individual` THEN 200000 ELSE 600000

-- s 40B "infringement offence means any of the following: (a) an offence
-- against section 40(1) of failing to comply with a suspension of supply
-- notice issued under section 33D: (b) an offence against section 40(1B)
-- involving the contravention of section 28 ...: (c) ... section 28B(2) or
-- (3) ...: (d) ... section 36C ... 36D ... 36L ... 36U ... 36WB ... 36WC".
-- The fee is prescribed, not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 40B
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an infringement offence` p IF
       p EQUALS `s 33D a suspension of supply notice`
    OR p EQUALS `s 28 a consumer information standard`
    OR p EQUALS `s 28B disclosing trader status online`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36C or 36D layby disclosure`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36L uninvited direct sale disclosure`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36U extended warranty disclosure`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36WB a gift card expiring in less than 3 years`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36WC a gift card without a prominent expiry`

@ref s 40B
`the most an infringement fee may be` MEANS 2000

-- ss 46E, 47F, 47J: other offences.
@ref s 46E
`the maximum fine for breaching a management banning order` MEANS 60000

@ref ss 47F(2), 47J(2)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstruction or for not complying with a s 47G notice, by` kind MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `an individual` THEN 10000 ELSE 30000

§§ `Orders under s 43 (ss 43A, 43B)`

-- s 43A "A person may apply ... for an order under section 43 at any time
-- within 3 years after the date on which the loss or damage, or the
-- likelihood of loss or damage, was discovered or ought reasonably to have
-- been discovered."
@ref s 43A
GIVEN discovered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for a s 43 order, loss discovered` discovered MEANS
    `add years` discovered 3

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the High Court`
    `the District Court`
    `the Disputes Tribunal`

-- s 43B "(1) The District Court must not make an order under section 43 if a
-- value or amount ... exceeds $350,000 or, if greater, the amount specified
-- in section 74 of the District Court Act 2016. (2) The Disputes Tribunal must
-- not make an order ... if a value or amount ... exceeds whichever is the
-- greatest of the following: (a) $60,000: (b) the amount specified in
-- section 10(1A)(b) of the Disputes Tribunal Act 1988." The amounts in the
-- other Acts are inputs. The High Court has no limit (s 37(d)).
@ref ss 37, 38, 39, 43B
@export Who may make an order under s 43 of the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ) for a given value: the High Court always; the District Court up to $350,000 (or the District Court Act amount, if greater); the Disputes Tribunal up to $60,000 (or the Disputes Tribunal Act amount, if greater). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN value IS A NUMBER  @desc The value or amount of the order (s 43B(3))
      `District Court Act amount` IS A NUMBER  @desc The amount in s 74 of the District Court Act 2016
      `Disputes Tribunal Act amount` IS A NUMBER  @desc The amount in s 10(1A)(b) of the Disputes Tribunal Act 1988
GIVETH A LIST OF Forum
`who may make a s 43 order of` value `, District Court Act amount` `District Court Act amount` `, Disputes Tribunal Act amount` `Disputes Tribunal Act amount` MEANS
    append (LIST `the High Court`)
           (append (IF value AT MOST max 350000 `District Court Act amount` THEN LIST `the District Court` ELSE EMPTY)
                   (IF value AT MOST max 60000 `Disputes Tribunal Act amount` THEN LIST `the Disputes Tribunal` ELSE EMPTY))

§§ `Management banning orders (ss 46C, 46D)`

-- s 46C(1)(a) "has, on at least 2 separate occasions within a 10-year
-- period ..., done either or both of the following: (i) committed an offence
-- against section 40(1) or (1A): (ii) been a director of, or concerned in the
-- management of, an ... body when it committed an offence against section
-- 40(1) or (1A)". (2) and only if "necessary to protect the public".
@ref s 46C
GIVEN first IS A DATE, second IS A DATE, necessary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a management banning order, occasions on` first `and` second `, necessary to protect the public:` necessary IF
        necessary
    AND NOT first EQUALS second
    AND (    (first LESS THAN second AND second AT MOST `add years` first 10)
         OR  (second LESS THAN first AND first AT MOST `add years` second 10))

-- s 46D "for a period specified in the order, which must be no more than 10
-- years".
@ref s 46D
`the longest a management banning order may last, in years` MEANS 10

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 1-3, 5, 5B, 6, 8, 12B, 18, 25-27, 28A, 29, 30A, 30B, 31(1)-(1A), 31(3A)-(4), 31A(3)-(5), 32(1)-(5), 33-35, 36A, 36C(1)-(2), 36D, 36E, 36G, 36J, 36L, 36N-36R, 36S, 36T, 36U, 36W, 36WA, 36WC, 36X-36ZC, 36ZE, 37-39, 40(2), 40A, 40C-40H, 41, 42, 43, 44-46B, 46F-46H, 46J, 46M, 47-51; Schedule 1AA cls 1-2; Schedules 1-3
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 1-3 title, purpose, interpretation, conduct outside New Zealand", "s 5 Crown corporations", "s 5B Takeovers Code", "s 6 Commission functions",
         "s 8 matters for unconscionable conduct (an input)", "s 12B matters for substantiation (an input)", "s 18 (no text)", "s 25 Part 1 provisions independent",
         "s 26 false trade descriptions on imports", "s 27 consumer information standards made by regulation", "s 28A fund-raiser disclosure regulations",
         "ss 29, 30A, 30B product safety standards and policy statements", "s 31(1)-(1A), (3A)-(4) unsafe goods declarations", "s 31A(3)-(5) recall notice contents",
         "s 32 compulsory recall powers", "s 33 imports prohibited", "ss 33A-33C product safety officers", "ss 34, 35 services safety standards",
         "s 36A purpose of Part 4A", "ss 36C, 36D, 36L, 36U disclosure contents (an input)", "s 36E risk in layby goods", "s 36G supplier cancellation grounds",
         "s 36J layby priority in insolvency", "ss 36N-36R enforcement and effect of cancelling a direct sale", "s 36S regulations", "s 36T, 36WA definitions",
         "s 36W regulations", "s 36WC gift card expiry statement", "ss 36X-36ZC, 36ZE auction definitions, start and end, notice, CGA exclusion, withdrawing bids",
         "ss 37-39 jurisdiction", "s 40(2) aggregate fines", "s 40A commercial gain", "ss 40C-40H infringement procedure", "ss 41, 42, 43 injunctions and orders",
         "ss 44-46B defences, servants and agents, findings, undertakings", "ss 46F-46H banning procedure and declaration applications", "s 46J standard form contracts (an input)",
         "s 46M examples of unfair terms", "ss 47-51 Commission powers, overseas regulators, financial products, savings, China",
         "Schedule 1AA cls 1-2 unfair contract terms transition", "Schedules 1-3 amendments and repeals"
